        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Unplug, disconnect the console cable first, then remove the
            console and uprights, and stop there unless you have a reason to go further.</strong>
            Photograph every stage, bag and label every set of bolts, and keep two people on every
            lift. The motor, control board and deck rarely need to come out.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Reassemble in reverse with the bolts snug before tightening, check the cable is not
            pinched, and test at low speed with the safety key before anyone uses it. If you are
            dismantling the treadmill to get it to a new home, our guide on
            <a href="/how-to-move-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">how to move a treadmill</a>
